{#- testing/remote_harness/templates/macros/controller_seed.j2 -- GENUINE, PARAMETERIZED Jinja macros that emit the
    managed-controller seed (POSIX sh) from the declarations:
      bs   = profile remote_harness.controller.bootstrap   (pins, artifacts, os_tools, budget, layout, refusals)
      ctl  = profile remote_harness.controller             (expect_core)
      lock = the file named by remote_harness.controller.lock_file_rel (wheels + collections)
    The seed is a BUILD OUTPUT rendered by package.yml into a local bundle; it is never committed.
    Every system executable is emitted through x(bs, name) = bs.os_tools[name].path (SEED-07b): an undeclared
    tool is a render error, a changed path changes the invocation. Every declared value reaches the shell
    through shq() (single-quote serialization); runtime values (root, generation path, op id) are the ONLY
    double-quoted expansions. Pure Jinja (no Ansible-only filters); block tags stay at column 0 so the
    ansible.builtin.template render (trim_blocks) and the lookup('template') render agree.
-#}
{%- macro shq(v) -%}
'{{ v | string | replace("'", "'\\''") }}'
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro cmt(v) -%}
{{ v | string | replace('\r', ' ') | replace('\n', ' ') }}
{%- endmacro -%}

