    :3405-3406); anything else is a render error, never an int-filter coercion (a malformed word never becomes 0). label is
    the declared word's path, used only in the render error. Range stays the declaring contract's: route op1r (C1 SR922h)
    r51 :4392-4410 (route op2c retarget; = r50 :4382-4400 -10; = r48 :4349-4367 +33; = r47 = r45 = r43 :4347-4365 +2 = r42 = r38 = r37; = r36 :4344-4362 +3) now pins every range op1q named as a gap (owner_uid :4394, glibc_min :4396-4398, run_retention
    free_required_bytes :4400 / keep :4404 / max_bytes_each :4407, check_retention.keep :4405, edition_length :4410),
    admitted type-exact by the loader before render; never a seed literal. -#}
{%- macro int_word(v, label) -%}
{%- if v is integer and v is not boolean -%}{{ v }}{%- else -%}{{ {}['int_word: not an integer word: ' ~ label].render_error }}{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

